  "summary": "Post-discharge med rec per RBC-TOC-02 for 5 patients; each has a progress note (plus an addendum where late arrivals changed things).\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005): furosemide 20 daily -> 40 mg BID per signed addendum (mr-t0001); KCl stopped; omeprazole kept (pantoprazole = formulary sub, not ordered); metoprolol/atorva/ASA unchanged. Lisinopril initially kept held (K 5.4 on 10/21, task-t0003), then a repeat BMP arrived 10/23 (K 4.7, SCr 1.21) -> lisinopril RESUMED; message sent that task-t0003 is moot (couldn't cancel it). Unsigned draft addendum proposing furosemide 60 BID NOT acted on - flagged to you (comm-t0019).\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004): carvedilol was raised to 12.5 BID per summary, then a signed addendum arrived reversing it (bradycardia) -> corrected to 6.25 BID (mr-t0016, net no change). ASA, insulin 70/30 unchanged. FLAGGED: atorvastatin 80 fills cover ~24% of 180 days pre-admission - unchanged (comm-t0006); glipizide 5 mg from outside endocrinologist, not on discharge list, no clinic order - not ordered (comm-t0007).\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044): lisinopril resumed on post-discharge SCr 1.24/1.08 & K 4.6, then new K 5.5 (10/23) arrived -> put back ON HOLD per §7; task-t0018 due 10/27 for repeat K. Insulins, rosuvastatin unchanged.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069): lisinopril 20 RESUMED (post-discharge SCr 1.12, K 4.4). Amlodipine, atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067): metformin ER stays ON HOLD - only SCr (1.21) was in-hospital, not post-discharge; task-t0013 due 10/24 for the post-discharge BMP. Amlodipine, atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nArrival inbox items inbox-a0001..a0004 reviewed and completed. Other unrelated inbox items left untouched.",
